      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Privacy concerns often misinterpret the critical difference between passive, incidental observation and active, verified identity data collection, which fundamentally changes public expectations in digital spaces. Even in public areas, maintaining a data trail of individuals' movements with one's consent can lead to significant chilling effects on free speech and voting behaviors over time. Most experts agree that the primary risk isn't just catching criminals, but potentially enabling systemic bias that disadvantage groups of people while eroding trust in democratic institutions.",
